e">5</text><title>1531: Antwerp opens its new commercial exchange</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="492.9" x2="492.9" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="492.9" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="492.9" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1585: Alexander Farnese captures Antwerp; the Dutch close the Scheldt</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="567.1" x2="567.1" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="567.1" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="567.1" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1648: The Peace of Münster confirms the split of Brabant between Spain and the Dutch Republic</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>1795: The French Republic annexes the duchy</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1183 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1795 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1190</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-schwabisch-hall">Diet of Schwäbisch Hall</a> confirms <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry I</a>'s ducal rank over Brabant</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1288</span><span class="rf-text">John I wins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> and gains the Duchy of Limburg</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1356</span><span class="rf-text">Duchess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joanna-duchess-of-brabant">Joanna</a> and Wenceslaus swear the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joyous-entry-of-1356">Joyous Entry</a> charter</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1430</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good of Burgundy</a> inherits Brabant</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1531</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> opens its new commercial exchange</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1585</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alessandro-farnese-duke-of-parma">Alexander Farnese</a> captures <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> close the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1648</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-munster">Peace of Münster</a> confirms the split of Brabant between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1795</span><span class="rf-text">The French Republic annexes the duchy</span></li></ol>
